	//
	// Sends one unauthenticated MCP initialize request to url (no identity token, no header) and follows the MCP authorization spec (2025-11-25) as a client would; the 401 challenge's resource_metadata (else the well-known protected-resource URIs; path form, then root), the resource metadata's authorization server, then its metadata (RFC 8414 path insertion, OpenID Connect path insertion, OpenID Connect path appending; the two root forms for an issuer without a path). Every request goes through the address guard and the internal-network allowlist (no proxy, no redirects, 5 s each, responses of at most 64 KiB, at most 8 requests). Nothing is stored or audited. Problems found (resource or issuer mismatch, no PKCE S256, ...) are reported in the result with status 200, not as errors. machineOAuth says whether the authorization server lists client_credentials in grant_types_supported, with its token endpoint (for authMode machine_oauth). 422 url_not_allowed as for create. 409 team_archived. 429 slow_down (10 a minute per person).
