// requirement: omit to keep, null to remove (capability overrides with mode scopes go back to inherit; so do they when the provider changes). A newly chosen provider must be enabled (422 provider_not_found) and open to the server (422 provider_not_allowed: restricted, and neither the server's team nor the server is on its access list); a turned-off one, or one that stopped being open to the server, can be kept (its calls are refused until the list is fixed). 400 invalid_scope (details.scope). Under approval_required, a published server goes back to pending when its URL changes or its requirement widens what any capability receives (a provider where there was none, another provider, or a scope not in effect before), audited as mcp_server.publish_request with reason url_changed or requirement_changed. Removing or narrowing a requirement never needs review.
//
